WEBVTT

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:03.630
Papa... Please save Lupin!

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:09.990
So Enzo's missing daughter... 
the one who was kidnapped is...

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:14.660
In a way, I'm responsible 
for the creation of PeopleLog.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.010
Lupin's weakness is his "family."

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.660
Just as PeopleLog predicted.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:33.680
Wait, Papa!

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.030
I'm Ami Enan.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.970
I'm the daughter you had with Yuko Enan!

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.080
What happy news, Enzo!

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:47.200
You betcha. Our PeopleLog app
managed to take down Lupin!

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.390
That's not what I meant.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:53.020
Your daughter's alive, man.

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:54.980
Oh, that.

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.410
That's all you can say?

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.300
Stop trying to act tough.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:03.110
Didn't you create PeopleLog 
for the sake of your daughter?

00:01:03.110 --> 00:01:06.010
You know what? I think that 
might've been the catalyst, sure.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:08.510
But now? It's irrelevant.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.030
Mama's dead!

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.120
Is she?

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:14.710
You didn't know?

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.000
Well, she <i>was</i> my ex, after all.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.450
What were you doing?

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:22.680
You didn't come to her funeral!

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.510
You never even looked for me!

00:01:24.990 --> 00:01:27.700
Doesn't saving the world 
make a bigger difference

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.020
than rescuing one kidnapped child?

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.030
Lupin! You're under arrest!

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.480
What the hell is going on here?

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.780
Lupin III is being arrested.

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:46.940
And the age of heroes is coming to an end!

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:14.960
<b>Just Then, An Old Buddy Said Something</b>

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.470
A toast! To the capture of Lupin III!

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:29.480
They finally got that bastard, Lupin.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:31.840
I heard one of his gang betrayed him.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:32.970
What a joke!

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:35.200
Looks like Lupin's been arrested.

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.480
But he's just gonna break out again, isn't he?

00:03:40.260 --> 00:03:42.490
There's no point in running anymore.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.130
You can run all you want,

00:03:46.130 --> 00:03:48.480
but PeopleLog will know 
exactly where you're headed.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:52.730
There's nowhere in the 
world Lupin can hide now!

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:57.500
Hey, let's go down there 
and watch them lock him up.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:03:58.870
Good idea!

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:01.900
PeopleLog knows where 
they're sticking him, too.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:04.550
You're going nowhere!

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.650
PeopleLog knew where 
to find you two, as well!

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.940
<i>It's been two weeks since 
Lupin III was arrested,</i>

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.670
<i>and the ICPO is finally 
preparing to transfer him.</i>

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.520
<i>They took their time, didn't they?</i>

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.570
<i>Apparently, his injuries were so bad, they 
had to wait for his condition to stabilize.</i>

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:20.460
You there.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.580
Mind removing the head of your costume?

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.500
A known criminal has been spotted 
wearing a costume like yours,

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.540
so we just need to check your identity.

00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:32.030
Get back here!

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:37.040
Man, Lupin, what the hell 
has happened to the world?

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:47.660
Goemon.

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.430
What should I do with this?

00:04:50.710 --> 00:04:53.250
I have defeated Lupin.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.930
I am now the strongest in the world.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:59.860
I'll hold on to it, then.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.430
When you've served your sentence, 
you can have it back.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:08.910
Goemon!

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:12.270
Fujiko Mine!

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:13.440
Take a good look at Lupin.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.800
That's the only way you'll find
the answer you're looking for.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:20.330
Fujiko Mine, you're coming with us!

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:21.980
Fujiko.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:25.970
If you want, we can get the government to 
reject the ICPO's request to hand you over.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.300
Sounds good to me.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:30.320
I'll let you boys keep me in 
your little cage a while longer.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:33.400
Lupin will be back.

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:36.890
And he'll need a glittering prize to 
steal when he does show up, won't he?

00:05:37.220 --> 00:05:38.590
It won't happen.

00:05:38.590 --> 00:05:40.900
You can't put the genie back in the bottle.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:43.330
Lupin III and all master thieves like him

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.220
are nostalgic footnotes in history now.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.320
Ling, I've thought up some 
new prediction vectors

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.890
that we can cook up using 
Bayesian probability...

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:04.920
I don't really remember you all that well.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:08.500
And Mama never talked about you, 
so I thought it better not to ask.

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:11.340
It was never really a problem,

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:13.450
so I didn't try to find you.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:14.930
But...

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:18.650
Oh, my dear Amy!

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:20.100
I'm your father!

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.820
He pretended to be my father,

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:25.690
but he couldn't even pronounce my name right.

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.250
So I took potshots at him.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:30.010
Because I was angry as hell.

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:35.400
But it made me realize something.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:40.860
Deep down, I'd always hoped my <i>real</i> 
father would come for me someday.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:41.560
So—

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:44.380
Is this little monologue gonna
 go on for much longer?

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:48.670
Come back when you have 
a bullet-point version, yeah?

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.550
I'm very busy at the moment.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.790
Quit staring, pal.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:06.900
You're making me blush.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:08.110
Lupin...

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:10.160
Don't look so blue.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.400
I'm still alive and kicking.

00:07:13.090 --> 00:07:15.410
Yes... I suppose you are, Lupin.

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.220
Remember the last time this happened?

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:22.410
When that gal tricked you...

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:25.480
You fell for her, but it turned out
 she was a guy all along.

00:07:25.480 --> 00:07:28.890
You really are a magnet for trouble 
when it comes to women.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.640
Laugh, Goemon!

00:07:31.640 --> 00:07:34.440
Once something's over, 
you may as well laugh about it.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:37.930
Lupin!

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:41.140
I mean, what else can you do at a time like this?

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:11.370
Dammit.

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:13.090
He went this way!

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:14.120
Don't let him escape!

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:16.940
I don't even get time for a smoke break.

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:36.880
Only one bullet left...

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:17.070
After his arrest, Lupin's being
transported from Olig Island to Marseilles

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:19.660
From there, he'll be taken 
to ICPO HQ in Lyon

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:20.240
The container he's being transported in
is apparently custom-made for ICPO use

00:09:20.230 --> 00:09:21.830
This is some collar...

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:26.250
What was the decisive factor in catching 
the elusive Lupin III after all this time?

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:28.630
It's all thanks to the years of collaboration

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:32.520
between our organization and the 
police forces of our member states.

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:33.500
Sir, wait a second!

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:36.210
What are you saying?

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:38.940
Inspector Zenigata is the 
one who arrested Lupin!

00:09:38.940 --> 00:09:42.260
No one's denying that Zenigata 
contributed greatly to this investigation.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:46.240
A lot of people think that Lupin was 
only arrested thanks to PeopleLog.

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:48.400
It only had the data to predict 
Lupin's actions because

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.260
Inspector Zenigata 
was always on his tail!

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.380
His career has been stuck 
in a rut since the day

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.520
he was put on the Lupin investigation.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:58.690
Didn't you just force this case on him?!

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:01.350
Making him a dedicated 
Lupin investigator...

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:05.110
That's like telling a salesman to hawk 
something nobody would ever want!

00:10:05.110 --> 00:10:08.960
And in spite of it all, Lupin's finally 
in custody, and all you can do is...

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:10.680
That's enough, Yata.

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:13.790
Dealing with the press isn't our department.

00:10:13.790 --> 00:10:14.830
But, sir!

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:16.130
Let's head back.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:19.510
The job's not done until Lupin is behind bars.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:24.320
Yes, sir.

00:10:29.930 --> 00:10:31.310
Take a look at this.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:33.540
The greatest criminal mastermind 
of our age, Lupin III,

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.070
is being ferried away.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:38.360
<i>A large crowd of onlookers has 
turned out to see the convoy.</i>

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:45.180
Y'know, Yata...

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:48.970
I've been hunting Lupin for a long time now.

00:10:49.390 --> 00:10:52.480
Caught him a few times, too.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:55.090
And I wasn't the only one, either.

00:10:55.090 --> 00:10:58.800
But in the end, he'd always get away.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:01.090
That wasn't your fault, sir.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.710
What I want right now...

00:11:03.710 --> 00:11:06.950
...is for him to serve his debt to society,

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:09.110
and then, to share a drink with him.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:15.420
That's why, Yata, I have to 
take him down by the book.

00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:19.150
I need to make him realize 
that he's been beaten.

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:23.860
I need to arrest Lupin's heart.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:31.880
There appears to be a broken 
down car blocking the road.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:33.630
Stop the convoy.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:36.370
There's no chance of an ambush out here.

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:39.270
They're stopping the convoy.

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:40.390
Those idiots.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:46.400
Has something happened?

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:47.890
It's him.

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:50.090
He's here.

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:53.390
We need you to move your vehicle, sir.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.400
Daisuke Jigen!

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.770
Drop the gun and get down on the ground!

00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:14.230
Good grief.

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:16.150
Would it kill you to let 
me finish my cigarette?

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:17.280
I'm almost done.

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:18.910
What are you doing?!

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:20.260
He's all alone!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:21.640
If he's resisting, shoot him!

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:22.250
But, sir—

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:23.260
Give me that!

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.810
Daisuke Jigen!

00:12:24.810 --> 00:12:27.840
Cooperate or else I'll be forced to...

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:52.330
Looks like one gun isn't enough.

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.140
Lupin.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:14.230
Yeah. It's Jigen, all right.

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:17.230
Can you help me up, Goemon?

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.520
Yata, we need to get out there.

00:13:23.520 --> 00:13:24.490
Understood!

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.650
Hey, Jigen. 'Preciate the rescue.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:09.070
Don't you think it's about time 
you hung up your hat, Lupin?

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:11.160
What are you talking about?

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.160
Retirement, Lupin.

00:14:18.070 --> 00:14:20.760
I hate to admit it, but that Enzo guy's right.

00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:22.160
Times have changed.

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:25.670
Yeah. You might have a point.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:27.740
If I'm brutally honest,

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:31.190
there's a lotta crap going on now 
that I have trouble keeping up with.

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:34.560
I prefer it when things are simple.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:41.220
Lupin, I've been running with 
you longer than anyone else.

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:42.340
Yeah.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:46.800
I figure I'm the only one who can 
talk you into calling it a day.

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.690
It sure as hell ain't gonna be Fujiko.

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:05.210
"Just then, an old buddy 
said something to him."

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:07.130
"Said it was time to retire."

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:09.840
"The enemy was fierce!"

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:13.680
"Possibly the strongest 
adversary he'd ever faced!"

00:15:14.080 --> 00:15:16.210
"His friends were all hurt,

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:19.220
and had lost their will to fight."

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:21.380
"What will happen to Lupin III?!"

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:24.700
"Does he have a plan for 
getting out of this one?!"

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:26.730
Give it a rest, Lupin.

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:29.510
Lemme ask you something, Jigen. 
With that kind of setup...

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:31.130
...can't you just hear it?

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:32.840
The sweet tunes, I mean.

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:34.320
"Tunes"?

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:38.550
Y'know, that achingly cool number that plays

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:40.800
when the hero's about to turn the tables.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:45.220
Life isn't some kind of TV show, Lupin.

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:47.600
We oughta make it one, then.

00:15:47.600 --> 00:15:49.250
Say what?

00:15:49.250 --> 00:15:52.470
There's only one person in the 
audience of your life: yourself.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:57.780
So what's the point if you don't care 
what happens next in the story?

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:00.380
"This is one hell of a tight spot!"

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:03.090
"Can he even get out of it?!"

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:05.380
"Maybe these bad guys are just too tough!"

00:16:05.380 --> 00:16:08.400
"How can he possibly beat 'em?!" Like that.

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:11.690
I wanna look forward to what I do next.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:16.690
And what if the ending doesn't 
turn out how you want?

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:19.260
"Goddammit!"

00:16:19.260 --> 00:16:21.030
"Got my hopes up for nothing!"

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:23.650
"Guess I'll have to leave the 
comeback for some other time."

00:16:23.650 --> 00:16:26.660
And what if the damn 
comeback never happens?!

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:30.170
Then, the audience loses 
interest and switches off.

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:34.520
And that's why, Jigen, until 
the day the story finally ends,

00:16:34.520 --> 00:16:37.170
I wanna keep being Lupin III.

00:17:00.590 --> 00:17:03.990
Lupin, I think I'm starting to hear it, too.

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:06.790
My own personal soundtrack.

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:18.740
You agree, don't you?

00:17:22.210 --> 00:17:24.790
Where the hell has Lupin gone?

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:27.240
It's been a month and 
they still have no leads.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:29.720
No hits on PeopleLog, either.

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:31.290
It just isn't possible.

00:17:31.290 --> 00:17:34.740
Did Lupin III turn into the
Invisible Man or something?

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:39.230
There's been no sign of Lupin III 
anywhere on the internet.

00:17:39.230 --> 00:17:43.650
What the hell kind of trick 
did you pull, Lupin?

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:45.740
Could it be...

00:17:48.620 --> 00:17:50.690
Maybe he's dead.

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:52.970
There's no way that's true!

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:58.000
And you believe in him, too.

00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:02.120
You're more romantic than 
I gave you credit for.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:05.530
Waiting for your prince to come 
and rescue you like this...

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:07.700
Well, for adults...

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:11.710
Sometimes, we need a bit of romance.

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:15.960
I've got all the money 
and fame I could ever want.

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:17.020
But...

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:21.290
Someone's posted on Lupin's PeopleLog.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:22.730
It's from...

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:25.040
Lupin III?!

00:18:27.030 --> 00:18:29.050
There he is! It's Lupin!

00:18:30.460 --> 00:18:31.540
Finally!

00:18:31.540 --> 00:18:33.530
The little bastard was
 still alive, after all!

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:37.540
"President Jack King and the oil companies 
have been colluding illegally"?!

00:18:37.540 --> 00:18:39.140
Lupin posted this?

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:42.310
Is there any truth to this secret deal?!

00:18:42.310 --> 00:18:44.400
PeopleLog gave it an A-rating!

00:18:44.400 --> 00:18:45.890
You can't lie your way out of this one!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.300
Get your ass out here, Mr. President!

00:18:53.080 --> 00:18:54.960
It's not just America he's targeting...

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:58.060
China, France, India, the Saudis...

00:18:58.060 --> 00:19:01.570
They're all in uproar about
Lupin airing their dirty laundry.

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:05.800
PeopleLog has given every exposé 
written by Lupin an A-rating.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:11.570
So PeopleLog has given 
Lupin its approval, huh?

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:15.740
<i>The FCC is looking into 
regulating PeopleLog.</i>

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:18.010
<i>Russia's threatening to deport 
Shake Hands personnel</i>

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:20.590
<i>if PeopleLog isn't shut down!</i>

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:23.280
<i>We're being hit by an 
onslaught of cyber attacks!</i>

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:25.250
<i>Considering the scale, 
a government must be behind it!</i>

00:19:25.250 --> 00:19:27.440
<i>The EU Parliament is talking 
about excluding PeopleLog</i>

00:19:27.440 --> 00:19:29.430
<i>from their net neutrality regulations!</i>

00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:31.940
Tell them all that we're dealing with it!

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:34.610
If we get bogged down in 
details, we'll get nowhere!

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:39.110
I guess you steal more 
than just loot, Lupin III.

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:40.960
This is bad, Enzo.

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:44.030
Lupin's using PeopleLog to rile up
countries around the world.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.460
We should at least take his posts down!

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:47.420
Not happening.

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:49.610
Don't you care that the 
company might go under?!

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:51.920
You're talking about killing PeopleLog.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:56.120
Collecting objective data in 
one place is PeopleLog's whole deal.

00:19:57.620 --> 00:20:00.220
You've really done a number on us, Lupin III.

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:02.630
But where are you hiding?

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:33.160
Hey, Jigen. Goemon.

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:35.210
Got this from the old man.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:37.000
It's Rebecca's response.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.170
I have also prepared the fishing rod.

00:20:39.530 --> 00:20:42.170
All right. Let's get this show on the road.

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:45.070
Here we come, Enzo.

00:20:45.070 --> 00:20:48.340
Your story is about to get its climax.

00:22:16.510 --> 00:22:18.500
Am I amazing or what?

00:22:18.500 --> 00:22:22.180
I was able to avoid the entire world 
and disappear into thin air!

00:22:22.180 --> 00:22:25.710
Looks like PeopleLog doesn't 
know me as well as they'd hoped.

00:22:25.710 --> 00:22:29.560
The name's Lupin III, and I know 
this sounds a little egotistical,

00:22:29.560 --> 00:22:33.920
but I'm the enigmatic master 
thief who can steal <i>anything</i>!

00:22:33.920 --> 00:22:35.830
Wanna know more?

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:37.990
Then, make sure you watch the finale!

00:22:37.990 --> 00:22:41.210
Next time: Viva Lupin III.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:45.000
<b>Viva Lupin III</b>

00:22:41.210 --> 00:22:43.380
You know where to watch it!
